---
import PolicyLayout from '../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How we handle information when you visit this website or contact us about appliance services."
>
  <section>
    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      Gavyn Appliances is a service name used by Gavyn Robinson, an individual appliance service
      provider serving the Greater Toronto Area and Barrie, Ontario. It is not an incorporated
      company. Gavyn Robinson operates this website and is responsible for handling privacy
      questions and service inquiries.
    </p>
    <p>
      This policy covers gavynappliances.ca, including its www address, and information provided
      through its service request form or related email and telephone conversations.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Information we receive</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Service requests:</strong> your name, email address, optional phone number, city or
        postal code, appliance choice and message. Your message may include an appliance brand,
        model or other details you choose to provide.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Follow-up conversations:</strong> information you provide when discussing the work,
        including a service address and appointment details if needed to arrange a visit.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Technical information:</strong> Cloudflare processes connection and request
        information, which can include an IP address, browser information, requested page, request
        time and security events, to deliver and protect the website and provide traffic statistics.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Please provide only what is relevant to your request. Do not send payment card details,
      passwords, identification documents or other sensitive information through the form. The
      website does not provide accounts or online payment processing.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>What we use it for</h2>
    <p>
      We use your information to answer questions, confirm service availability, discuss pricing,
      arrange requested work and communicate about that work. Related records may be needed for
      follow-up, warranty matters, accounting, resolving disputes or meeting legal obligations.
      Technical information helps keep the website available, detect abuse and understand its
      overall traffic.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not sell your personal information or use service inquiries to build advertising
      audiences. There is currently no newsletter or marketing-message programme.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      Submitting the form asks us to use the information you provide to handle your request,
      including delivery through the providers described below. The phone number is optional.
      Without the required contact and request details, we may be unable to respond or arrange
      service. You can contact us by email or telephone instead.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may ask us to stop using your information for a purpose you previously agreed to. We will
      explain any consequences, such as being unable to continue arranging a visit, and any legal or
      contractual restrictions that apply. Consent to receive marketing is not a condition of
      requesting service.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Who processes the information</h2>
    <p>
      Gavyn Robinson reads and handles incoming inquiries. The website also relies on service
      providers:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Cloudflare:</strong> hosts and protects the website, processes form submissions
        through a Pages Function and provides traffic statistics.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Brevo:</strong> delivers service requests as transactional emails. The submitted
        details are included in the email; delivery-related records may also be processed.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Gmail:</strong> receives and stores the service-request email and related
        correspondence in the business mailbox.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      There is no separate customer database in this website application, but emails and provider
      records can still contain personal information. Providers process information under their
      applicable terms and policies. Information may also be disclosed where required by law or
      where legally permitted to address fraud, security incidents or legal claims.
    </p>
    <p>
      These services may process or store information outside Canada, including in the United States
      or other countries. Information there may be subject to those countries’ laws and lawful
      access by their authorities. No Canada-only storage commitment is made.
    </p>
    <p>
      Provider information:{' '}
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a>,{' '}
      <a href="https://www.brevo.com/legal/privacypolicy/">Brevo Privacy Policy</a> and{' '}
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>How long information is kept</h2>
    <p>
      We keep inquiries and correspondence only while needed to handle the request and related
      service matters. We review retained information periodically and delete information that is no
      longer needed. There is no blanket indefinite retention period.
    </p>
    <p>
      The appropriate duration depends on whether the inquiry is still active, whether work took
      place, any relevant warranty or dispute, and applicable accounting or legal requirements.
      Records needed for those purposes may be kept longer than an unanswered or completed inquiry.
      Deletion is managed by the operator, not an automatic website timer; provider logs and backups
      follow the relevant provider’s retention and deletion processes.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Protecting information</h2>
    <p>
      The website uses HTTPS, server-side form validation and a basic spam trap. The Brevo API key
      is held on the server rather than sent to visitors’ browsers. Access to inquiry handling is
      limited to the operator and the service providers involved in processing. No internet
      transmission or email service can be guaranteed completely secure.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Access, correction and privacy concerns</h2>
    <p>
      You can contact Gavyn Robinson using the details below to request access to your personal
      information, ask how it has been used or shared, correct an inaccuracy, request deletion or
      raise a concern. We may need proportionate information to verify your identity before
      releasing or changing records. Please do not send identification documents unless we have
      discussed a safe way to verify the request.
    </p>
    <p>
      We respond to access requests within the time required by applicable law, generally 30 days
      under PIPEDA. If a permitted extension or exception applies, we will explain it. Deletion
      requests are considered alongside outstanding service needs and legal obligations; deletion is
      not unconditional.
    </p>
    <p>
      If a concern remains unresolved, you can contact the{' '}
      <a href="https://www.priv.gc.ca/en/report-a-concern/">
        Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Cookies, external links and updates</h2>
    <p>
      Read our <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a> for information about browser storage,
      traffic statistics and Cloudflare security features. Facebook and Instagram are external
      links, not embedded feeds; visiting them is subject to their own privacy practices.
    </p>
    <p>
      We update this policy when relevant practices change and revise the effective date above.
      Where a new purpose requires consent, publishing an updated policy alone does not replace that
      consent.
    </p>
  </section>
</PolicyLayout>
